    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d401">

                <pb facs="0432" n="356" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg356"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.51/520</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Haiti to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of Haiti</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-06-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 28, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: I have the honor to
                    inform your excellency that the President of Haiti has agreed to the proposition
                    made by the President of the United States to appoint Mr. A. J. Maumus as
                    Receiver General and Mr. W. S. Matthews as Deputy Receiver General of the
                    Customs of the Republic of Haiti.</p>
                <p>The President of Haiti hopes soon to have the opportunity and pleasure of also
                    appointing the Financial Adviser as provided by Article II of the Convention of
                    September 16, 1915, between the Republic of Haiti and the United States of
                    America.</p>
                <p>Be pleased, [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Solon Ménos</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
